          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>General anaesthesia is defined by four components. Which of the following is NOT</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>General anaesthesia is defined by four components. Which of the following is NOT one of them?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Amnesia</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Amnesia IS one of the four components. The defining quartet is unconsciousness, analgesia, amnesia, and complete muscle relaxation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Anxiolysis</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Anxiolysis (relief of anxiety) is a feature of sedation, not one of the four pillars of general anaesthesia. The defining quartet is unconsciousness, analgesia, amnesia, and muscle relaxation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Muscle relaxation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Complete muscle relaxation IS one of the four components. It enables surgical access and controlled ventilation under general anaesthesia.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Unconsciousness</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Unconsciousness IS one of the four components, distinguishing general anaesthesia from lesser levels of sedation.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The four components are unconsciousness, analgesia (freedom from pain), amnesia, and complete muscle relaxation. Anxiolysis belongs to sedation, not general anaesthesia."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Well done. The four pillars — unconsciousness, analgesia, amnesia, and muscle relaxation — define general anaesthesia and guide the choice of every drug used."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
