          "label": "<p>A patient requires an MRI-guided biopsy under general anaesthesia. Which precaut</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A patient requires an MRI-guided biopsy under general anaesthesia. Which precaution is specific to the MRI environment?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>A dedicated trained anaesthesia provider must remain present throughout</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A dedicated provider is a standard NORA safety requirement for ALL remote locations, not specific to MRI.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Pulse oximetry and capnography must be continuously available</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Continuous pulse oximetry and capnography are mandatory monitoring for general anaesthesia in any location — operating theatre or remote site.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Only MR-conditional monitors, laryngoscopes, and gas cylinders may enter the suite</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The strong magnetic field in an MRI suite makes standard ferromagnetic equipment a projectile hazard. Only monitors, laryngoscopes, and gas cylinders certified as MR-conditional may be brought inside.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>A written emergency protocol must be available and rehearsed before the procedure</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A rehearsed emergency protocol is required for ALL NORA locations, not specifically for MRI.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "All four options describe genuine safety measures, but only MR-conditional equipment is specific to MRI. The other three — dedicated provider, monitoring, and emergency protocols — apply to every NORA location equally."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly right. While all NORA locations require equivalent monitoring, personnel, and protocols, the MRI suite adds a unique ferromagnetic hazard that restricts every piece of equipment entering the room."
                }
              ],
